In the second block of the sequential binary logistic regression model, a collection of behavioral and attitudinal factors pertaining to cell phone usage while driving was incorporated with the demographic and vehicle-related predictors from Block 1 to assess the model's improved predictive capability. Table 5 indicates that multiple variables from the initial block retained statistical significance. The type of vehicle
license (p = 0.024) was a significant predictor, demonstrating that drivers with public or commercial licenses were over twice as likely to utilize mobile phones while driving in comparison to those with private licenses. Similarly, vehicle type (p = 0.005) and model year (p = 0.021) exhibited significant correlations, indicating that older or more frequently utilized automobiles are associated with increased


